-- SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
-- risk: additive
--
-- #2873 (ADR 0047) -- an assistant can run the setup guide, with the
-- person's confirmation for every change and never with a credential.
--
--   reads   get_setup_status      the one setup status (0539) with, per
--                                 step, what an assistant may do, the next
--                                 milestone and step, and the levels
--           list_setup_levels     the levels and presets (the app's table)
--           preview_setup_levels  what a choice switches on and off; no write
--   writes  apply_setup_levels    the levels, through set_feature_flags with
--                                 its read-set (0245), after confirmation
--           mark_setup_step       a manual step done or an optional one set
--                                 aside (0545's rules), after confirmation
--
-- A credential is never taken from an assistant: an argument named like
-- one is refused (DKS01, `secret_in_app_only`) before anything is asked or
-- run, and a step that holds one (`secret` in the step catalogue) is never
-- acted on for an assistant. The confirmation stores the proposal with the
-- revision it was computed from (the workspace's stored features, or the
-- step's state); a proposal whose revision moved is stale, never applied.
--
-- mcp_confirm (0412) and mcp_confirm_action (0272) are restated whole (no
-- anchored patch has touched either): the target both read comes from
-- mcp_target_of, which finds an operation's own mcp_target_<id> by name and
-- falls back to mcp_target (0272 and its anchored patches 0289-0291,
-- untouched). mcp_confirm also answers a refused credential or an absent
-- feature as a refusal, not as invalid arguments; mcp_confirm_action takes
-- a target that can no longer be read as changed.

